    "description": "A kingdom based in north central Anatolia, established during the collapse of the Achaemenid empire by the Mithridatid dynasty. In the early first century BC, under Mithridates VI, it expanded to encompass Cappadocia and most of the Black Sea coast, challenging Roman control of Asia and Greece in a series of four wars.",
